# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Static Shoals
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Two sand bars under a sky that never clears, four radio masts strung with cable shouting static on every band, and the Fleet's last radio barge beached on the main bar.
island on.arrive=message||Static on every band at once. Four masts stand over two grey sand bars, their red lights turning.

note teonote Teo's note | TEO - on the back of a Fleet logbook page\n\nThe Fleet's way south ends here. Most of them turned back at the static. I do not blame them; it gets into your teeth, and then into your dreams, and my dreams were bad enough already.\n\nSomebody has to keep the masts lit so the boats can find their way home, so it is me. Hedda said she would wait for me at the wall. Ines went ahead with the radio, because of course she did.\n\nThe engine plans are in the chest - the Fleet's mechanics drew them from what they found in the masts. Mast 4 has a hut. Ride the cable, and do not look down; I looked down.\n\nIf you find tobacco, it was mine. Review of the Static Shoals: no stars. Too loud.\n\n- T. Varga
note fleetchest Fleet chest | The Fleet's chest: the engine control plans the mechanics drew, and a zipline handle for the cable to mast 4.
note mast4chest Mast 4 hut | A chest in mast 4's hut: a metal detector's plans, the static crackling in its coil.
note flarelocker Flare locker | The masts' flare locker: a firework's plans and a box of dry rockets.
note workshop Mast workshop | The workshop under mast 3: a zipline base's plans, for the cable crews.
loot fleetchest Blueprint_EngineControls*1;ZiplineTool*1;Scrap*4
prop fleetchest loot.refill=0
loot mast4chest Blueprint_MetalDetector*1;Battery*1;CopperOre*2
prop mast4chest loot.refill=0
loot flarelocker Blueprint_Firework*1;Plastic*4;Rope*2
prop flarelocker loot.refill=0
loot workshop Blueprint_ZiplineBase*1;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*2
prop workshop loot.refill=0

note barchest Washed-up crate | A crate washed up on the bar, sealed in tar: it kept dry.
loot barchest Scrap*6;Plastic*4;Battery*1;Rope*2
note radiomanpage Radioman's last page | The last page of a radioman's pad, under a stone on the far bar:\n\nSTATIC ON ALL BANDS. NOT WEATHER.\n\nIt comes from the masts. The Concord built them to drown the pulse so nobody would follow it - and it worked for thirty years. We had a dance on the barge when the pulse went quiet in the static. I danced with the cook. He trod on me.\n\nThen last month an old man came through in a dory and asked me which band the static was strongest on. He sat all night with my set, and in the morning there was a hole in the static exactly the shape of the pulse. I do not know how he did it. I am going to follow the hole.
note shoalcavechest Speaker cave chest | A chest under the humming speaker: wire, a coil, and a battery still half charged.
loot shoalcavechest Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1;Copper*2;Bolt*2
prop shoalcavechest loot.refill=0
note netbook Net house book | THE FLEET'S NET HOUSE - catch book, last page\n\nNo fish since the static started. Not one.\nThe nets come up clean and the needle on the barge's set points south.\nThe Fleet sails tomorrow to see what scares the fish. Teo stays to keep the masts lit.\n\nThe radio on our table still works if anyone gets the generator going. The part is in the mechanic's box by the humming cave.
note spotterlog Spotter plane log | SPOTTER PLANE LOG\n\nFlew the Fleet's course south ahead of the boats.\nThe static on the Receiver turned to a voice for a moment - numbers, read out slowly, in no language I know.\nLost the horizon in the grey. Put down on the north bar. The Fleet never saw my flare.
# (deep pass 10-24: the climb and the dive)
story genpart2|Coil pack|Battery|A coil pack for the net house generator, sealed in a drowned van. One of its three parts.
story chainkey|Chain key|Bolt|A heavy key on a ring, stamped CONCORD WELL. One of the five that open the chained door of the Command Well, deep under the calm circle.
note ssdivechest Coil room | A sealed coil pack, tagged FOR THE NET HOUSE.
loot ssdivechest story:genpart2*1;Plastic*4;Scrap*3;Rope*2
prop ssdivechest loot.refill=0
note sstop Wiring room locker | The coil fits the card: a chain key and a spark plug.
loot sstop story:chainkey*1;TitaniumOre*2;CircuitBoard*1;Bolt*3
prop sstop loot.refill=0
prop sstop obj.name=sstop
prop sstop if.open=has|story:genpart2|1
prop sstop else.open=message||The wiring room locker. A wiring card on the lid matches a coil pack - you don't have one.
note ssstash Cable reel | A bag of spares tied to a cable reel.
loot ssstash Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1;Nail*6
prop ssstash loot.refill=0
note ssdivesecret Radioman's tool tray | A radioman's pliers and solder, put away neatly.
loot ssdivesecret MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*1
prop ssdivesecret loot.refill=0
note sscairn Static cairn | A cairn on the dune peak, a radio headset hung on it, and a page of Ines's radio log:\n\nIf you listen long enough the static is a voice. Teo says so, and for once Teo is right.\n\nThe old man again, clear as anything with the masts so loud: Five posts. Five keys. Five pairs of hands. Calling, calling. He knows our names now. He said Hedda's. He said mine.\n\nI have not told Hedda. She would turn us round, and I cannot turn round. Not with the pulse this close.\n\nSouth of here the Receiver shows a wall across the sea, and a gate in it. Hedda waits there. I am going on to meet her. - I.
note ssplan Cable store floor plan | FLEET CABLE STORE - painted on a board by the door\n\nCoil room, wiring room, reels. Keep the door shut. Mind the dark.\n\nScratched under it, by someone who came out again: left hand on the wall, all the way, and you will see every room. It took me an hour. Do not drop your light; the floor eats lights. Teo had to come in after me and he has not let me forget it.\n\n- H.
note keeperss Keeper's log: Static | KEEPER'S LOG. Static Shoals - oilcloth, tacked to the cable store door:\n\nThe Concord drowned her in noise. Four masts, shouting nonsense day and night, so that no one would hear the Well calling its crew. Thirty years they shouted. They did not reckon on a keeper who has listened to one light for forty.\n\nI cut a hole in the static the shape of her call. It took a night and most of my patience. Now the pulse goes out clean and the pilgrims follow it like ducklings.\n\nI am sorry about the boy at the net house. He keeps the masts lit for a fleet that is not coming back. That is a keeper's sort of foolishness. I recognise it.\n\nThe wiring card is in the dark store, with a key. Bring a light. I could not; my lamp is for her.\n\n- S.W.
note heddass Hedda's watch | CAPTAIN'S WATCH - Hedda's capitals, on a page left in the net house\n\nTeo is staying. He says the boats need the masts. The boats are not coming back, and he knows it, and he is staying anyway. I have never been prouder of a fool.\n\nI gave him my good knife. He cried, which he will deny, and so will I.\n\nInes walks about with her ear to the set and does not sleep. Something talks to her on it. She thinks I have not noticed. I notice everything; it is my only skill.\n\nTomorrow I go south to the wall to look for a way through. Ines will follow when she has listened enough. I have left the coil pack where the Fleet keeps its cable - in the dark store by the peak. Whoever you are: mind the dark.
quest title=Static
quest intro=A beached radio barge on a grey bar, static from every mast. Look in the barge.
step read|Teo's note|1|Read Teo's note in the radio barge
step blueprint|Blueprint_EngineControls|1|Take the engine control plans from the Fleet chest
step kill|Screecher|4|Drive the screechers off the masts
step reach|mast_4|1|Ride the cable from mast 1 to mast 4's hut
step blueprint|Blueprint_MetalDetector|1|Take the metal detector plans in mast 4's hut
step blueprint|Blueprint_Firework|1|Take the firework plans from the flare locker under mast 2
step read|Net house book|1|Read the catch book at the ruined net house on the south bar
step open|Mechanic's toolbox|1|Find the mechanic's toolbox by the humming cave in the east bar
step collect|story:teovoice|1|Start the net house generator and listen to its radio
step open|Supply drop|1|Open the supply drop the voice gave away, by the spotter plane
step reach|ss_maze|1|Find your way into the dark cable store by the dune peak
step collect|story:genpart2|1|Find the coil pack in the cable store's coil room
step open|Wiring room locker|1|Open the wiring room locker deep in the cable store
step blueprint|Blueprint_ZiplineBase|1|Take the zipline base plans in the workshop under mast 3
quest done=The masts are yours, and so is the static. Beyond it, on the Receiver: a wall, and a gate in it.
quest reward=Rope*6;Scrap*6;CopperOre*2

save Static Shoals
